WEBVTT

00:00.830 --> 00:02.480
Rawr!

00:02.830 --> 00:06.580
It's time to start the main event 
of the game's eighth event!

00:06.580 --> 00:09.440
I'm going to explain the 
rules now, so listen close!

00:09.440 --> 00:12.800
<b>8th Event 
Main Event 
Event Period: 3 Days (In-Game)</b>

00:09.840 --> 00:12.220
The event period will be three in-game days.

00:12.220 --> 00:14.820
For those participating at 
the highest difficulty level,

00:14.820 --> 00:19.410
the last ones standing at the end 
will receive five silver medals!

00:19.410 --> 00:20.630
Oh! Here!

00:20.630 --> 00:24.780
We're all participating at the highest 
difficulty, just like we planned!

00:24.780 --> 00:28.170
Uh, I don't think Dorazou can hear you.

00:28.170 --> 00:34.010
You can also get medals by defeating 
strong monsters or finding hidden items!

00:34.010 --> 00:34.950
And...

00:35.370 --> 00:39.810
Medals you earn will be immediately 
distributed to all your party members!

00:40.210 --> 00:42.780
If the medals are shared between us...

00:42.780 --> 00:48.010
It might be more effective to gather 
medals separately than to work together.

00:48.010 --> 00:51.030
Of course, it'd be safer to 
stick together, though...

00:51.030 --> 00:56.990
Also, super strong monsters will appear 
at certain times during the event.

00:56.990 --> 01:00.830
Watch the timer to get an idea 
of when this will happen!

01:01.270 --> 01:04.160
The map will be the same one 
used in the preliminary.

01:04.430 --> 01:05.900
I thought so.

01:05.900 --> 01:06.920
Huh?

01:06.920 --> 01:10.120
And now, it's time for the countdown!

01:10.120 --> 01:10.880
Ten!

01:10.880 --> 01:13.900
What should we do, Sally? 
Keep everyone together,

01:10.880 --> 01:19.720
Nine! Eight! Seven! Six! 
Five! Four! Three! Two!

01:13.900 --> 01:16.470
or gather medals separately?

01:16.470 --> 01:19.740
Let's think about that after 
we get a look at the situation.

01:19.740 --> 01:21.970
One! Zero!

01:21.970 --> 01:24.610
Off you go!

01:27.290 --> 01:36.110
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:54.150 --> 02:56.030
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:56.670 --> 03:01.380
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>Setting Up a Base</b>.

02:59.250 --> 03:02.430
Oh, good! We've got a nice, 
clear view from here!

03:02.780 --> 03:05.590
Doesn't look like any 
other players are around.

03:10.870 --> 03:12.980
They didn't waste any time showing up!

03:15.170 --> 03:17.430
So these are our first opponents!

03:18.270 --> 03:20.010
[Loving Sacrifice]!

03:20.500 --> 03:22.740
Faye, [Strengthen Item]!

03:24.690 --> 03:27.220
Syrup! [Spirit Cannon]!

03:27.220 --> 03:29.060
Tur...

03:29.060 --> 03:30.890
...tle!

03:31.340 --> 03:32.250
Tsukimi!

03:32.250 --> 03:33.060
Yukimi!

03:33.060 --> 03:34.100
Bear!

03:34.610 --> 03:37.320
[Power Share]! [Bright Star]!

03:37.560 --> 03:39.780
Bear!

03:43.660 --> 03:45.860
We couldn't take them down in one blow?!

03:45.860 --> 03:47.530
Well, this <i>is</i> the highest difficulty!

03:47.530 --> 03:50.120
Haku! [Super Megamorph]! [Paralysis Poison]!

03:50.860 --> 03:52.670
Oboro! [Binding Barrier]!

03:53.000 --> 03:54.540
Snake!

03:55.420 --> 03:56.990
Snake-ake!

04:04.470 --> 04:05.590
Necro!

04:05.590 --> 04:06.970
[Flames of Death]!

04:09.470 --> 04:10.720
[Double Strike]!

04:10.720 --> 04:12.260
Bear!

04:14.190 --> 04:17.900
We did it! Our monsters are all so strong!

04:18.120 --> 04:21.360
Having your protection made 
it easy to fight, Maple!

04:21.620 --> 04:24.360
But didn't something feel kind of strange?

04:24.360 --> 04:26.590
Like we had too much power.

04:26.590 --> 04:28.370
Now that you mention it...

04:30.010 --> 04:31.820
Sou, over here.

04:31.820 --> 04:33.660
Huh?! Is that me?!

04:33.660 --> 04:36.790
I borrowed your attack power a bit.

04:37.130 --> 04:39.420
It was just as powerful as I expected.

04:39.420 --> 04:44.270
I see. Sou can copy our 
appearances and abilities.

04:44.270 --> 04:47.640
Awesome! So that's what Sou can do!

04:47.640 --> 04:49.850
It wasn't [Double Strike]...

04:49.850 --> 04:52.310
It was [Triple Strike]!

04:52.310 --> 04:53.820
Pretty cool, huh?

04:54.150 --> 04:56.750
The transformation doesn't last long, though,

04:56.750 --> 04:58.950
and it has a long cool-down time.

04:58.950 --> 05:00.970
Sally? What's wrong?

05:00.970 --> 05:04.490
Hmm... They didn't drop any medals.

05:04.490 --> 05:09.450
I guess that means those monsters were 
among the weaker ones in this event.

05:09.450 --> 05:12.830
It might not be so easy 
to get medals this time.

05:13.090 --> 05:15.290
Okay, let's do a quick review.

05:15.510 --> 05:19.400
Our goal is for us to collect 
a total of ten medals

05:19.400 --> 05:22.200
and trade them for rare skills and items.

05:22.200 --> 05:24.890
If we survive until the 
end, we'll get five medals.

05:24.890 --> 05:30.010
That means our guild as a whole needs 
to gather five additional medals.

05:30.010 --> 05:32.200
Hmm, I guess so...

05:32.200 --> 05:34.320
So what do we do?

05:34.320 --> 05:37.730
Work together, or split up?

05:37.730 --> 05:40.650
For starters, how about 
we split into two groups?

05:40.650 --> 05:42.870
Keeping in mind how well our 
skills work together, of course.

05:42.870 --> 05:44.190
Sounds good to me.

05:44.190 --> 05:47.240
It's probably safer than 
sending everyone out alone.

05:47.570 --> 05:51.650
I guess anyone with low defense 
should team up with Maple.

05:51.990 --> 05:53.410
That'd be me, and...

05:53.700 --> 05:55.690
May and Yui!

05:55.690 --> 05:57.510
Thanks for having us!

05:57.510 --> 05:59.250
Let's do our best, Sis!

05:59.250 --> 06:03.840
And that means the remaining 
four of us will be a team.

06:03.840 --> 06:07.470
With Sou on our side, we won't 
be lacking in offensive power.

06:08.010 --> 06:10.940
Party members are displayed on the map,

06:10.940 --> 06:15.180
so we can split up for now and get back 
together when the strong monsters show up.

06:15.180 --> 06:17.850
We'll head toward the forest, then.

06:17.850 --> 06:20.200
Maple, your group can cover the wetlands.

06:20.200 --> 06:21.500
Got it!

06:23.780 --> 06:28.140
This is... a pretty unique ride.

06:28.140 --> 06:29.320
You get used to it.

06:29.560 --> 06:32.070
Moving is a lot faster this way, too.

06:32.070 --> 06:36.170
I like it. Haku feels nice and cool.

06:36.660 --> 06:39.550
Haku, we're not too heavy for you, are we?

06:39.550 --> 06:40.650
Snake, snake.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.080
He's so cute!

06:43.410 --> 06:46.040
There's no competition 
between guilds this time,

06:46.040 --> 06:47.760
so we can focus on gathering medals.

06:48.090 --> 06:50.830
The field is really big this time, though.

06:50.830 --> 06:52.720
Where should we even look for them?

06:53.950 --> 06:56.250
I thought this might come up.

06:56.250 --> 06:57.930
I'm sending you a map. Check it out.

06:58.150 --> 07:02.740
I marked all the spots I found during 
the preliminary that looked suspicious.

07:02.740 --> 07:04.650
I sent it to the other team, too.

07:04.650 --> 07:06.670
Way to go, Sally!

07:07.000 --> 07:10.110
Let's see... We're right here now, so...

07:10.110 --> 07:12.420
Hey, there's a marker on the wetlands.

07:12.420 --> 07:13.590
Oh, there is!

07:13.590 --> 07:16.230
Yep. So how about we head there first?

07:16.230 --> 07:18.680
Got it! Tsukimi!

07:18.680 --> 07:19.360
Yukimi!

07:19.360 --> 07:20.330
Bear!

07:24.650 --> 07:26.770
What do you think, Sally?

07:26.770 --> 07:30.380
There weren't any monsters like 
this here in the preliminary.

07:30.690 --> 07:33.210
The terrain looks the same, though...

07:33.210 --> 07:35.600
It does look like there's something here.

07:35.860 --> 07:37.380
What should we do?

07:37.740 --> 07:41.790
We can't afford any deaths, so it might 
be dangerous to just jump right in.

07:41.790 --> 07:43.060
It'll be fine!

07:43.060 --> 07:44.670
At a time like this...

07:46.590 --> 07:49.400
It sure is handy being able to fly!

07:49.400 --> 07:52.440
Syrup! Bring us in!

07:52.440 --> 07:53.870
Turtle...

08:00.570 --> 08:02.580
Syrup, return!

08:05.290 --> 08:06.900
We're underground?

08:07.620 --> 08:09.860
Under that little island, I guess?

08:11.740 --> 08:12.720
Incoming!

08:15.390 --> 08:16.770
[Loving Sacrifice]!

08:16.770 --> 08:19.330
We might be able to handle 
them with elemental attacks!

08:19.330 --> 08:20.810
Use fire!

08:20.810 --> 08:21.430
Right!

08:21.430 --> 08:23.440
Let's finish this quick, Sis!

08:24.660 --> 08:27.320
[Double Strike]!

08:34.990 --> 08:37.620
With Maple's [Loving Sacrifice] in effect...

08:37.620 --> 08:39.870
None of its attacks can hurt us!

08:43.410 --> 08:45.250
I can't fall behind!

08:45.250 --> 08:46.810
[Fireball]!

08:49.530 --> 08:50.750
One more time!

08:57.510 --> 09:00.180
Wow! Nice going, you guys!

09:00.180 --> 09:02.290
Wait! Something's not right!

09:03.210 --> 09:03.890
What?!

09:04.170 --> 09:06.120
May! Yui! Your feet!

09:06.120 --> 09:07.100
Huh?!

09:15.370 --> 09:17.150
Thank you so much!

09:17.150 --> 09:19.000
Maple, bring out Syrup!

09:19.000 --> 09:20.490
You two, come with me!

09:26.710 --> 09:29.610
So when they come back 
to life, they multiply?

09:29.610 --> 09:33.690
What do we do? If we go back down, they'll 
attack us with those vines again.

09:33.690 --> 09:34.900
It's okay!

09:34.900 --> 09:36.450
We've been practicing.

09:36.450 --> 09:39.010
We can attack even from this far away!

09:39.640 --> 09:41.100
Ready, and...

09:42.180 --> 09:45.430
Let's... go!

09:48.810 --> 09:50.870
All right! Perfect hit!

09:50.870 --> 09:52.770
Our practice paid off!

09:52.770 --> 09:54.850
Ooh, nice!

09:54.850 --> 09:57.800
I bet attacking with your Great 
Hammers would do even more damage!

09:57.800 --> 09:59.780
Actually, it wouldn't.

09:59.780 --> 10:01.990
They just break the iron balls.

10:02.370 --> 10:05.790
We've asked Iz to make tougher ones for us.

10:06.570 --> 10:07.710
I see...

10:14.200 --> 10:16.840
There's nothing for us to even do...

10:16.840 --> 10:19.330
I'm starting to feel sorry for the monsters.

10:24.850 --> 10:27.560
Silver Medal

10:24.850 --> 10:27.560
All right! We got a medal!

10:27.820 --> 10:30.500
Oh, Maple's group got a medal.

10:30.500 --> 10:32.150
Didn't take them long, as usual.

10:32.150 --> 10:36.860
We should be reaching one of the marked 
points on Sally's map soon, too.

10:36.860 --> 10:39.030
Hey, I bet that's it.

10:40.630 --> 10:43.660
There doesn't seem to be anything around...

10:43.890 --> 10:45.770
Should we try touching it?

10:45.770 --> 10:47.080
I think so.

10:47.080 --> 10:48.420
Haku, do it.

10:50.040 --> 10:51.030
Snake.

10:57.420 --> 10:58.800
Haku, return.

10:58.800 --> 10:59.860
Necro!

10:59.860 --> 11:00.770
Fay!

11:00.770 --> 11:01.430
Sou!

11:05.780 --> 11:06.760
[Cover]!

11:11.900 --> 11:13.700
Kanade, you're up!

11:13.700 --> 11:14.520
Sou!

11:18.150 --> 11:21.460
Thank you, Sou! I'll heal you now.

11:24.360 --> 11:26.760
Seems to be a ninja-type monster.

11:27.260 --> 11:29.480
It won't show itself willingly.

11:29.890 --> 11:33.650
It's definitely out there 
somewhere. What do we do?

11:33.650 --> 11:37.340
I know what might work, as long 
as no obstacles are in the way.

11:37.720 --> 11:40.590
All right. I'll take care of it.

11:41.090 --> 11:43.180
You will? What're you gonna do?

11:51.730 --> 11:54.450
You're using some dangerous-looking 
stuff again...

11:54.450 --> 11:58.450
I'm gonna detonate them all at once. 
Everyone stay within the safety zone.

11:58.950 --> 12:00.570
Might want to stick closer together.

12:01.250 --> 12:02.700
Here we go!

12:03.000 --> 12:05.820
Three, two, one!

12:18.540 --> 12:19.590
Kanade!

12:19.590 --> 12:21.130
I got this!

12:21.130 --> 12:22.550
[Searcher's Sun]!

12:30.750 --> 12:31.680
Found 'em!

12:31.680 --> 12:32.720
Let's go!

12:32.720 --> 12:33.850
[Super Speed]!

12:33.850 --> 12:36.690
[Last of Sword - Hazy Moon]!

12:37.590 --> 12:39.070
[Ghost Mud]!

12:39.070 --> 12:41.300
Necro! [Flames of Death]!

12:49.620 --> 12:52.230
All right, that's our second medal.

12:49.620 --> 12:54.620
Silver Medal (2)

12:52.230 --> 12:54.620
Two on the first day... I'd say 
we're in pretty good shape.

12:55.110 --> 12:57.740
That took longer than I expected, though.

12:58.060 --> 13:00.670
We might want to go ahead and regroup.

13:00.890 --> 13:04.190
Looks like the strong monsters 
will be coming out at night.

13:04.190 --> 13:07.220
Okay, let's join back up 
with Maple's group, then.

13:12.040 --> 13:14.680
Oh, there they are! Hey!

13:14.680 --> 13:16.770
Maple!

13:16.770 --> 13:18.980
Is this the place?

13:20.150 --> 13:22.980
What do you think? Perfect 
for a base, isn't it?

13:23.410 --> 13:25.950
It looks sort of dungeon-ish...

13:26.340 --> 13:27.820
But nothing's jumping out at us.

13:27.820 --> 13:31.550
Yeah. It's probably a dummy dungeon 
put here to confuse players.

13:31.550 --> 13:35.250
It may be here to provide 
a resting point, as well.

13:36.750 --> 13:41.030
Check out how big it is. Should 
be a comfortable stay, right?

13:41.030 --> 13:42.300
Good point.

13:42.300 --> 13:45.300
We'd better get this place set 
up before nightfall, then!

13:45.860 --> 13:48.070
I'll start working on furniture right now.

13:48.070 --> 13:49.510
Thanks a lot!

13:49.510 --> 13:53.120
I think I'll go set some 
defensive traps, then.

13:53.120 --> 13:55.060
We'll help you!

13:55.060 --> 13:56.580
Okay, then...

13:56.580 --> 13:58.500
We'll get to work somewhere else.

13:58.500 --> 14:01.060
Good idea. We don't have much time.

14:01.060 --> 14:04.290
We should split up and rig 
some defense mechanisms first.

14:04.290 --> 14:06.650
All right! Let's get started!

14:06.650 --> 14:08.030
Yeah!

14:08.740 --> 14:10.950
That being said...

14:11.190 --> 14:13.450
What can we actually do?

14:13.450 --> 14:15.210
This place is huge,

14:15.210 --> 14:18.670
and we need to make sure nobody 
can get through here, so...

14:19.000 --> 14:20.130
I know!

14:20.520 --> 14:22.140
[Venom Capsule]!

14:27.140 --> 14:29.930
Hmm... I don't think this is enough.

14:29.930 --> 14:32.850
If we're attacked, the 
whole room will collapse.

14:33.170 --> 14:34.220
I know!

14:34.820 --> 14:36.210
Hup!

14:42.690 --> 14:46.990
Now I just need to make sure poison 
can't come in from the rear of the cave!

14:46.990 --> 14:48.650
[Throne of the Heavenly King]!

14:52.320 --> 14:54.780
There! All done!

14:57.900 --> 14:59.830
How's it going for you guys?

14:59.830 --> 15:01.060
Oh, Maple!

15:01.060 --> 15:02.900
Watch where you step!

15:02.900 --> 15:03.670
Huh?

15:08.340 --> 15:10.510
Maple!

15:17.620 --> 15:19.090
That scared me!

15:19.090 --> 15:21.520
Oh, no! I ruined the trap you set!

15:21.520 --> 15:23.200
That's okay!

15:23.200 --> 15:26.310
I'm just glad you're all right, Maple.

15:26.310 --> 15:29.240
I'm so sorry. I'll help you rebuild it.

15:30.660 --> 15:34.200
I gotta be more careful when 
I check out the other rooms.

15:34.200 --> 15:38.630
We've set them up so we can all get 
past them as long as we walk carefully.

15:38.630 --> 15:41.670
So they shouldn't be a problem 
when we leave, either.

15:43.290 --> 15:46.130
Oh, no! The room I was just in!

15:46.130 --> 15:48.590
I made it so nobody can get through!

15:49.380 --> 15:53.260
I messed up! I gotta redo 
it so we can get in and out!

15:53.260 --> 15:55.880
Wh-What sort of room did you make?

15:55.880 --> 15:58.180
I'll show you guys later.

15:58.760 --> 16:00.500
Let's finish up here first.

16:00.500 --> 16:01.550
Okay!

16:06.110 --> 16:09.220
Incredible! It looks so pretty in here!

16:10.540 --> 16:14.780
Oh, welcome back. Are you 
done setting up traps?

16:14.780 --> 16:16.660
Yeah! Everything's set!

16:16.660 --> 16:18.580
All the preparations are done!

16:19.390 --> 16:23.480
Iz, it looks like you didn't 
do anything to this half.

16:23.480 --> 16:25.660
That's in case the monsters get in.

16:25.660 --> 16:28.880
Some of them might manage to slip 
through the traps, after all.

16:31.250 --> 16:32.600
There we go.

16:34.050 --> 16:38.420
Th-This is amazing. It must have 
required lots of materials.

16:38.420 --> 16:41.430
I didn't use much that was valuable.

16:41.430 --> 16:44.550
I'd still like you to help 
me restock later, though.

16:44.550 --> 16:45.380
Sure!

16:45.380 --> 16:47.170
We can help out anytime!

16:47.170 --> 16:48.110
Whoa!

16:48.110 --> 16:50.820
You went crazy again!

16:50.820 --> 16:53.840
Welcome back. You guys all done, too?

16:53.840 --> 16:57.450
Yes. We'll have to be careful 
when we leave here, though.

16:57.760 --> 17:01.830
There are a lot of traps that'll kill 
you if you trip them by mistake.

17:01.830 --> 17:06.180
Wait! What if other players 
wander in here without knowing?

17:06.180 --> 17:07.460
They'll get hurt!

17:07.460 --> 17:09.960
Don't worry. We put up a sign outside.

17:09.960 --> 17:13.340
Maple Tree's Main Base 
Dangers at Every Turn   Enter at Your Own Risk

17:10.390 --> 17:13.340
No one who can actually read 
will be coming in here.

17:13.340 --> 17:17.760
Maple Tree's Main Base 
Dangers at Every Turn   Enter at Your Own Risk

17:13.970 --> 17:15.210
What kind of sign?

17:15.670 --> 17:16.970
This kind.

17:17.760 --> 17:19.880
Well, I suppose it's not wrong.

17:19.880 --> 17:23.480
I'd say it couldn't be more right, in fact.

17:23.480 --> 17:26.870
That's true. The place is filled with traps.

17:26.870 --> 17:27.900
Still...

17:27.900 --> 17:30.650
I do kind of wish we could 
test some of them out...

17:35.700 --> 17:38.270
Maple Tree Base
 Map

17:36.050 --> 17:38.280
So this is what the whole place looks like?

17:38.660 --> 17:42.410
It's more like a fortress 
than a base at this point.

17:42.410 --> 17:44.970
We can't let our guard down, though.

17:44.970 --> 17:47.620
We don't know what kind 
of monsters are coming.

17:48.450 --> 17:49.990
Looks like it's about time.

17:49.990 --> 17:53.130
Time for those <i>really</i> strong 
monsters to come out!

17:53.130 --> 17:55.840
There's a chance it could get past our traps.

17:55.840 --> 17:59.050
Yeah. Let's get ourselves ready and stand by.

18:05.790 --> 18:07.330
Looks like it's started!

18:07.330 --> 18:10.940
Yeah. We need to be ready 
to attack at any time!

18:15.830 --> 18:17.090
Did it die?

18:17.460 --> 18:18.540
Very likely.

18:18.870 --> 18:22.700
We'll have to go out and 
check the traps to make sure.

18:22.970 --> 18:25.750
Should Maple and I go?

18:25.750 --> 18:28.830
Even if the monster's just 
playing dead to ambush us,

18:28.830 --> 18:30.380
we should be able to run back here.

18:30.670 --> 18:33.630
True. Even if the traps 
went off accidentally,

18:33.630 --> 18:35.840
we're safe as long as we've got Maple.

18:35.840 --> 18:39.550
Okay! We'll go check it out, then!

18:43.640 --> 18:44.870
Maple!

18:50.570 --> 18:53.480
This... is the really strong monster?

18:53.480 --> 18:56.570
Seems so... but...

18:58.900 --> 19:02.870
Aww. It tried so hard to stay alive.

19:03.170 --> 19:06.680
But the goal is for <i>us</i> to stay alive, right?

19:06.680 --> 19:07.830
We didn't have a choice.

19:08.690 --> 19:14.300
But this means the monster got 
past that trap, doesn't it?

19:14.620 --> 19:18.260
Yeah. A flying monster could've 
made it through that one.

19:18.260 --> 19:22.510
I guess that means we don't 
have enough anti-aerial traps.

19:23.610 --> 19:27.720
Look at all the materials! They're 
from the monster that just died!

19:28.490 --> 19:31.460
If this is the only trap we 
have to reset, that'll be easy.

19:31.460 --> 19:33.100
Let's all rebuild it together.

19:33.570 --> 19:34.680
Good idea!

19:34.680 --> 19:38.820
I want some good sleep tonight, so 
let's make sure our defenses are solid!

20:00.680 --> 20:02.910
That should keep us safe for now.

20:02.910 --> 20:07.010
Hey, Sally! It's still early, so 
why don't we do something fun?

20:07.310 --> 20:09.270
Sure. Like what?

20:09.270 --> 20:11.980
A game! You guys wanna play, too?

20:13.090 --> 20:14.900
What's the current status?

20:14.900 --> 20:17.240
Pretty much as we predicted,

20:17.240 --> 20:19.810
though the players who've 
tamed powerful monsters

20:19.810 --> 20:22.320
are having an easier time 
surviving than we expected.

20:22.320 --> 20:26.830
But that was the point of adding them. 
If anything, this is what we want.

20:26.830 --> 20:30.290
Looks like our enhanced night 
monsters put up a hard fight.

20:30.290 --> 20:33.100
The parties that took defensive 
measures against them

20:33.100 --> 20:35.540
didn't seem to take much damage.

20:35.540 --> 20:38.690
Nearly all the members of 
both Order of the Holy Sword

20:38.690 --> 20:41.730
and Flame Emperors are still alive.

20:42.040 --> 20:43.940
What's going on with Maple Tree?

20:44.750 --> 20:46.550
I'll put up the video feed.

20:59.930 --> 21:01.770
H-How in the world...

21:01.770 --> 21:04.260
They've created a whole dungeon...

21:04.260 --> 21:07.530
It's even more deadly than the ones we make.

21:07.990 --> 21:10.940
It's basically a tower defense game.

21:10.940 --> 21:12.870
Uh... What are Maple and her friends doing?

21:14.050 --> 21:16.170
They appear extremely relaxed.

21:16.170 --> 21:18.760
Like some evening on an overnight field trip.

21:18.760 --> 21:20.100
W-Well, I mean...

21:20.100 --> 21:24.110
We knew a monster enhanced to that degree 
still wouldn't be a match for them!

21:24.110 --> 21:26.760
The event's still just getting started!

21:26.760 --> 21:30.750
That's right! The monsters will 
get stronger and stronger!

21:30.750 --> 21:34.100
Even if they do, this gives Maple 
Tree too great an advantage.

21:34.710 --> 21:38.690
Shouldn't we have just made a simpler cave?

21:40.540 --> 21:45.400
Oh, but then it would be immediately 
clear that it was a dummy.

21:45.900 --> 21:48.220
I do think this was the right call.

21:48.220 --> 21:49.300
Right?!

21:49.300 --> 21:50.250
Yeah, yeah!

21:50.250 --> 21:51.120
That's right!

21:52.510 --> 21:55.210
The first day will be over soon.

21:55.580 --> 21:59.290
We shall have to carefully watch 
what they do on the second day.

